# ===========================================================================
# TRANSCRIPTION DISCREPANCIES
# ===========================================================================
#
# #1  sheet −40−, LOC 0408, line 1674.  The scan prints the OBJ column as
#     «3F28», but the source statement is «MVI A,40» and the opcode for
#     MVI A is 3Eh, not 3Fh (3Fh is CMC, which takes no operand). Moreover,
#     with 3Fh the byte 28h would be left dangling and the rest of the
#     programmer would shift, which the following LOC addresses contradict:
#     the next instruction is at 040A, so 0408 occupies TWO bytes.
#     Transcribed as 3E28. This is a scanning defect, not a listing error.
#
#     (General rule for this transcription: when the OBJ column and the
#     source column contradict each other, the one consistent with the
#     surrounding LOC addresses wins, and the discrepancy is recorded here.)

